abstract: >
  This repository introduces Intent-Driven Agentic CI/CD — a novel platform engineering
  paradigm in which application teams declare deployment intent via a structured contract
  (contract.yml), and an autonomous Agentic CI/CD Factory interprets that intent to decide
  what to deploy, which Terraform modules to invoke, which workflows to execute, and what
  governance and validation policies to apply. The framework decouples deployment intent
  from pipeline implementation, eliminating the need for application teams to author or
  maintain CI/CD pipelines. The architecture includes reusable GitHub Actions workflows,
  Copilot-integrated AI agents for Terraform scaffolding and security review, OIDC-only
  authentication (zero long-lived secrets), and multi-environment (dev/test/prod) promotion
  orchestrated entirely by the factory. This repository serves as the consumer reference
  implementation demonstrating the pattern against Azure infrastructure (Static Website,
  Key Vault, Resource Groups) via Terraform with remote state on Azure Blob Storage.
